    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-1452",
      "problem": "Sketch the graph of $y=-x^2+4x-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y=-x^2+4x-3.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=0,1,2,3,4$ and then use the formula $y=-x^2+4x-3$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-3$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/442d3550eb77f837da6875bc3877023db44f9f3ee862b433fa56d2186c352bd2.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/e95ebb53e7924dc1e99a92be85e6981def3c1186029c6c620bded4bb797f0c06.png)",
